		<description><![CDATA[Open source really embodies three changes from typical hierarchical human social systems.  Gift culture, the right to fork, and perpetually increasing levels of complexity.  But these pieces are not all new, what changed to make open source happen?  What problem is it actually solving? Gift culture is not new.  It is as old as currency.  [&#8230;]]]></description>
